inguish output callback counts from tokenizer counts. makeTokenAccumulator counts callback invocations, while Ollama supplies content chunks and separate final usage. Preserve legacy frames, but use an accurate declared unit for new measurements and keep analyze production unknown where unsupported.","In s4, document the live reporter seam during story design. The current runner reads TAP only after each file exits, and TapTitle retains title/depth rather than stable leaf identity. Add observation instrumentation without changing the isolated report destination, process ownership or exit semantics; qualify duplicate sibling titles, nested suites, retries and truncated reports.","For adapter qualification, verify that elapsed time, heartbeat activity and source sequence changes alone do not increment meaningfulRevision. Existing review trackers deliberately update observation metadata independently of completed work; retain that distinction when mapping snapshots. Tests were inspected as evidence and were not executed."]},{"chunkId":"vscode","status":"incomplete","summary":"The VS Code design aligns with the DEF on originating-chat delivery, attempt isolation, aggregate status, observer-independent retention, cancellation and project-scoped recovery. Current client contracts and relevant lifecycle tests were inspected. Visual verification of the generated UX mock remains incomplete.","findings":[{"id":"vscode-001","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/uxDefinition/body/2","message":"The unavailable-state example preserves the last measured counts but drops their measurement age, although its description says freshness is preserved. A user cannot distinguish recently verified measurements from substantially older ones. Retain an explicit as-of time or age in this state, consistent with the architecture's original-age guarantee and the upstream requirement.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json#/body/uxDefinition/body/2","docs/epics/show-long-