egated attempts, observer-free retention beyond idle/capacity limits, conversation removal followed by delayed events, project result recovery and pending cancellation. These are future implementation qualification targets; existing tests were inspected without execution.","Preserve stable task-row identity through append-only transcript persistence and paging. The current diff-row replacement scheme demonstrates an existing compatible approach."]},{"chunkId":"mcp","status":"passed","summary":"The MCP design aligns with the DEF at HLD level. It preserves execution authority and results, restricts notifications to valid request tokens, corrects the current notification-counter/stage-total mismatch, and assigns shared fallback arbitration to s1 and client delivery/qualification to s6. Fencing, cadence preservation, observer transfer, overlap suppression, bounded unchanged details and degraded recovery are addressed. No blocking defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/citations/5","/citations/13","/citations/14","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md: constraints k2–k5, k7–k8 and s6 acceptance criteria","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md: R4–R8, R17 and A4–A7","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts: mcpProgressSink","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts: no-token, monotonic counter, total and rejected-send assertions","src/mcp/server.ts: forward, review connection handlers, stdio lifetime and progressEventOf","src/mcp/forward-step.ts: progress forwarding, terminal envelope preservation and connection failure handling","src/mcp/__tests__/forward-step.test.ts: token forwarding, silent no-token completion and unchanged result envelope","src/mcp/__tests__/forward-step-features.test.ts","src/mcp/__tests__/daemon-stream.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["During implementation, update the existing total assertion alongside the forwarder: notification counts must not retain stage totals. Add request-completion and disconnect race coverage without changing operation results.","Carry the DEF's exact fallback disclosure, terminal stopping and separate Claude Code/Codex/Vibe capability checks into downstream qualification. Live host execution was not performed for this HLD review; current forwarding tests establish protocol behavior, not visible rendering or autonomous scheduling."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"All inventory units received substantive inspection across the five completed chunks. The current HLD and canonical artifact match the reviewed baseline, and their shared contracts, responsibilities and rollout align with the DEF. No additional cross-system defect was demonstrated. Existing findings remain recorded in their original chunks; mandatory companion rendering verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-hld.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","Checkpoint: completed architecture, foundation, producers, vscode and mcp feedback; inventory coverage has no undeclared units","Canonical/live comparison: summary, framework summary, architecture, all six shared contracts, all six story boundaries and non-functional targets","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/e