s/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/component-dependency.html could not be inspected because the browser access host was unavailable. Its embedded Mermaid source was inspected and matches the seven components and six dependencies in /body/componentDependencyDefinition; visual layout and successful browser rendering remain unverified."],"advice":["Add a compact predecessor mapping linking July stories #42, #43 and #44 to successor responsibilities s2, s6 and s5 respectively. Current traceability requires following the predecessor DEF and story documents.","Detailed ER and sequence verification belongs to the foundation chunk; detailed UX verification belongs to the VS Code chunk. Companion existence and linkage alone do not establish their visual correctness."]},{"chunkId":"foundation","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the DEF and relevant code. The foundation separates execution authority, observation, freshness and retention, and specifies fenced recovery and terminal persistence before delivery. Generated ER source contradicts the intended cardinalities. Mandatory visual verification remains blocked.","findings":[{"id":"foundation-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/erDefinition; docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html embedded Mermaid","message":"The generated ER model contradicts the ownership contract. `Invocation ||--o| Conversation` permits only one invocation per conversation, whereas sc1 and the Invocation.conversation description explicitly allow many invocations in one conversation. It also renders `Task ||--o{ Attempt`, allowing zero attempts despite the required, one-or-more attempts definition. Correct the relationship definitions or generation inputs and regenerate the companion so its cardinalities agree with the shared contracts.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json#/body/erDefinition/classes/Invocation/attributes/conversation",".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json#/body/erDefinition/classes/Task/attributes/attempts","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:56","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html: embedded Mermaid relationship declarations"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sharedContracts","/body/sharedContracts/0","/body/sharedContracts/1","/body/sharedContracts/2","/body/nonFunctional","/body/erDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/5","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/6","/citations/12","/citations/18","document:line:293","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-hld.json: architecture feedback and inventory","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md: lifecycle, observation and qualification requirements","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html: embedded Mermaid source","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid source","src/shared/types.ts: IpcStreamMessage and ProgressEvent contracts","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts","src/daemon/request-context.ts","src/daemon/server.ts: trusted connection identity, dispatch and disconnect handling","src/daemon/__tests__/connection-request-context.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/review-runtime-owner.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts: status projection and detached terminal handling","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts: capacity eviction","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/session-file-store.test.ts: persistence, stale writes and lifecycle coverage"],"limitations":["Actual renderings of docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/er-model.html and docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/sequence-diagram.html could not be inspected: the browser access host was unavailable and native Google Chrome access was denied. Their embedded sources were inspected, including all sequence participants and terminal persistence ordering; successful rendering, readability and layout remain unverified."],"advice":["During story design, make the authorization bridge explicit for reconnects and multiple windows. Existing TrustedRpcContext supplies a server-minted connection identity and daemon epoch, while client labels are untrusted; specify how a replacement connection establishes authorized access to retained project/conversation tasks.","Carry the stated qualification commitments into focused cases for terminal persistence failure, exhausted observation reservations, owner lease expiry, delayed prior-epoch callbacks and conversation removal during renewal. Existing transport and session tests provide useful seams but do not establish these future coordinator behaviors."]},{"chunkId":"producers","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected all assigned producer contracts and citations against the live HLD, DEF, upstream requirements, current implementations and relevant tests. No blocking design defect was demonstrated. The adapters preserve executor authority, distinguish supported measurements from unknown values, separate review coverage and publication, and retain test command outcomes independently of progress.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sharedContracts/3","/body/sharedContracts/4","/body/sharedContracts/5","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/15","/citations/16","/citations/17","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json: shared contracts, story boundaries, rollout and qualification targets","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md: k1–k3, k7 and stories s2–s4","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md: R2, R3, R9, R12 and A2, A3, A16, A17","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md: existing progress stream compatibility","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts: runStart, workflowProgressToStage and makeTokenAccumulator","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts: runStart, makeProgressEmitter and eventToProgressData","src/workflow/review/design-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/coverage-progress.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/checkpoint-progress.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/retry.test.ts: retry budgets and retained accepted feedback","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress-view.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts: task assignment, interruption and publication boundaries","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/progress.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/publication.test.ts: durable publication before terminal status","src/daemon/steps/build-step/validation-checks.ts: reporter isolation, runTestFile and runValidationChecks","src/daemon/steps/build-step/tap-results.ts","src/daemon/steps/build-step/__tests__/validation-checks.test.ts: malformed reports, output isolation, command failures and reporter-file failures","src/agent/providers/ollama.ts: output callbacks and final token usage evidence"],"limitations":[],"advice":["In s2, explicitly distinguish output callback counts from tokenizer counts. makeTokenAccumulator counts callback invocations, while Ollama supplies content chunks and separate final usage. Preserve legacy frames, but use an accurate declared unit for new measurements and keep analyze production unknown where unsupported.","In s4, document the live reporter seam during story design. The current runner reads TAP only after each file exits, and TapTitle retains title/depth rather than stable leaf identity. Add observation instrumentation without changing the isolated report destination, process ownership or exit semantics; qualify duplicate sibling titles, nested suites, retries and truncated reports.","For adapter qualification, verify that elapsed time, heartbeat activity and source sequence changes alone do not increment meaningfulRevision. Existing review trackers deliberately update observation metadata independently of completed work; retain that distinction when mapping snapshots. Tests were inspected as evidence and were not executed."]},{"chunkId":"vscode","status":"incomplete","summary":"The VS Code design aligns with the DEF on originating-chat delivery, attempt isolation, aggregate status, observer-independent retention, cancellation and project-scoped recovery. Current client contracts and relevant lifecycle tests were inspected. Visual verification of the generated UX mock remains incomplete.","findings":[{"id":"vscode-001","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/uxDefinition/body/2","message":"The unavailable-state example preserves the last measured counts but drops their measurement age, although its description says freshness is preserved. A user cannot distinguish recently verified measurements from substantially older ones. Retain an explicit as-of time or age in this state, consistent with the architecture's original-age guarantee and the upstream requirement.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json#/body/uxDefinition/body/2","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/ux-mock.html: unavailable-state text and element descriptions 10–14","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md:35","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md: R17, progress-source failure and original measurement age"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/uxDefinition","/citations/19","/citations/20","/citations/21","document:line:394","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/HLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/HLD-206db3426ffd4428.json: shared contracts, s5 boundary, UX definition and companion references","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md: k2–k8 and s5 acceptance criteria","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md: R1, R3, R8, R10–R17 and A11–A17","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md: legacy stream and reader compatibility","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/ux-mock.html: generated HTML source and element descriptions","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts: typed projection targets, transcript delivery, restoration and targeted actions","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts: append-only rows, concurrent writers, status persistence and capacity eviction","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts: transcript identities, progress epochs, pending requests and active-chat contract","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts: detached observer, status projection, restoration, error/Stop paths and view disposal","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts: distinct session ownership and idle eviction","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts: cross-chat stale-action isolation, concurrent turns and waiting-input precedence","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/session-file-store.test.ts: stale progress rejection, reload persistence and active/unresolved capacity protection","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/turn-lifecycle.test.ts: detach versus Stop and process-lease ownership",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-hld.json: completed chunk feedback and finding identifiers"],"limitations":["The actual rendering of docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/ux-mock.html could not be inspected because the browser access host was unavailable. Its generated HTML and canonical definition were inspected; successful rendering, layout, readability and control placement remain unverified."],"advice":["During s5 design, make every completion writer use the aggregate task-aware projection, including detached-observer reconciliation, setup failures and Stop. Current code has separate direct done transitions in these paths.","Extend the existing stale-turn and cross-window tests to cover delegated attempts, observer-free retention beyond idle/capacity limits, conversation removal followed by delayed events, project result recovery and pending cancellation. These are future implementation qualification targets; existing tests were inspected without execution.","Preserve stable task-row identity through append-only transcript persistence and paging. The current diff-row replacement scheme demonstrates an existing compatible approach."]},{"chunkId":"mcp","status":"passed","summary":"The MCP design aligns with the DEF at HLD level. It preserves execution authority and results, restricts notifications to valid request tokens, corrects the current notification-counter/stage-total mismatch, and assigns shared fallback arbitration to s1 and client delivery/qualification to s6. Fencing, cadence preservation, observer transfer, overlap suppression, bounded unchanged details and degraded recovery are addressed. No blocking defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/citations/5","/citations/13","/citations/14","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-pr